# E §10 readers-of, L §5.18 (tally 2.1.7 B2, issue #133; P64): each reader is an item listed once, at the
# first layer one of its nodes is met, a layer by id: a move whose day and amount read d is listed once (pay), and
# what reads the move is one layer below it (nfa, v). 2.1.6's refcore printed `pay, pay, v, nfa`, a move's day node
# as a reader of its own. (T's G11 ro_m.)
=== ro_m.tally
model ro
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index qs = [q1, q2]

kind fees: transfers

input amt: money PLN

input d: date

input rate[k in qs]: num

band tax(x: num): num

def fee[k in qs]: money PLN = round(amt * rate[k], minor(PLN), half-up)

def t: num = tax(1)

def total: money PLN = fee[q1] + fee[q2]

def b: money PLN = bal(konto, d + 1 day)

ask nfa: count(f in fees over 2026)

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: fees
  on d
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee[q1]

ask r_amt: readers-of amt

ask r_d: readers-of d

ask r_qs: readers-of qs

ask r_fees: readers-of fees

ask r_pay: readers-of pay

ask r_konto: readers-of konto

ask r_tax: readers-of tax

ask r_card: readers-of card_2026

ask r_src: readers-of card


ask r_total: readers-of total

ask r_self: readers-of r_amt

ask v: b, total, t

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  d = 2026-02-10
  rate[q1] = 0.1
  rate[q2] = 0.2
  tax: [0, 100) = 0.1 "low"
  tax: [100, inf) = 0.2
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect r_d r_amt r_konto
r_d: b, pay, nfa, v
r_amt: fee, pay, total, nfa, v
r_konto: b, pay, nfa, v
